.SH "NAME"
pcre2_convert_context_copy \- copy a convert context
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.sp
.ss \n[.ss]
.nf
.fam C
\fB\&#include\fP \fB<pcre2.h>\fP

\fBpcre2_convert_context\fP *pcre2_convert_context_copy(
      \fBpcre2_convert_context\fP *\fIccontext\fP);
.fam
.fi
.ss \n[.ss] 0
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.sp
This function is part of an experimental set of pattern conversion functions.
It makes a new copy of a convert context, using the memory allocation function
that was used for the original context. The result is \fBNULL\fP if the memory cannot
be obtained.
.sp
The pattern conversion functions are described in the
\f(CRpcre2convert\fP
documentation.